CM_ "Porsche 986/996 powertrain CAN (CAN1 of the VCU), 500 kbit/s. Reverse engineering master; mirrored by tools/generate_can_md.py. OPEN (986 #10): the original DME sends 0x280/0x289/0x298/0x4E0/0x7A0 every 10 ms, the VCU every 30 ms (5 slots x 6 ms); cluster works on the bench, timeouts in other control units unknown - decision and CAN capture needed. OPEN (986 #11): stationary log only (can_logs/986_log_stand.csv); record a driving log with braking, steering, indicators, cruise buttons and lights.";
CM_ BO_ 640 "0x280. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME (original DME 10 ms, VCU 30 ms). RPM scaling matches Teensy (raw = rpm*4). OPEN (986 #6): bit 4 toggles, byte 1 = 0x79 and byte 6 = 0x54 constant, not in the DBC; VW PQ Motor_1 reads bit 4 Time_Out_Bremsen_Botschaft, byte 1 inner torque, byte 4 inner torque without intervention, byte 6 mechanical loss torque, byte 7 driver torque request. Clarify bytes 1, 4, 6, 7 with the original DME at different pedal positions.";
CM_ BO_ 649 "0x289. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME. Layout from VW PQ Motor_2. Bit 24 always 1, bit 25 = speed limiter selected (VCU code). OPEN (986 #12): bits 0-5 carry four signals selected by MO2_Mp_Code (6|2) without a valid multiplexer declaration; strict DBC tools reject the file.";
CM_ BO_ 664 "0x298. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME. Several signals marked 'Turbo? Unsure' in the notes; Speed_raw scaling unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 680 "0x2A8. Wheel speeds, legacy 15-bit variant. Stationary log only: values not verified while driving.";
CM_ BO_ 416 "0x1A0. Bremse_1 (BR1) mapping. OPEN (986 #1): byte 6 (bits 48-55) counts up by 1 per frame, so BR1_MSR_Mo (and the VCU value itq_pct) is a counter, not a torque; BR1_Zaehler (56|4) low nibble constant 0xD, bits 57-58 toggle. OPEN (986 #12): BR1_ASRMo_fa and BR1_MSR_Mo_inv share byte 5.";
CM_ BO_ 1185 "0x4A1. BrakeNormal_or_Offset depends on the multiplex code (bits 30-31). OPEN (986 #2): bits 13-15 count 0..7 per frame, so ReceiptForACCMessage/DriverBraking/RegulatorError_FDR are a 3-bit counter; find the real driver-braking bit with a braking log. OPEN (986 #3): bits 45-47 and 61-63 change every frame (checksum or multiplexed content?), bit 29 always 1.";
CM_ BO_ 1248 "0x4E0. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME. Byte 0 status/lamp interpretation on bits 0..7 plus MO5 lamp/consumption layout on bits 9..31.";
CM_ BO_ 1296 "0x510. VehicleSpeed scaling/offset is a working hypothesis. Bits 24-27 are a 4-bit counter (stationary log). OPEN (986 #4): bits 40 and 43 always 1 (byte 5 = 0x09), meaning unknown.";
CM_ BO_ 1312 "0x520. OilPressure offset assumed 0. OPEN (986 #5): byte 2 bits 16-20 change slowly (0x4E..0x50; temperature or fuel level?); bits 0 and 22 always 1; Counter_Unknown (byte 5) rotates 0x12, 0x03, 0x30, 0x1D every 100 ms - check whether it carries the odometer multiplexed (VW PQ Kombi_3: Kilometerstand 40|20, Standzeit 24|15).";
CM_ BO_ 1088 "0x440. PRND mapping from notes: P=128, R=119, N=96, D=81, M=225. OPEN (986 #9): not in the stationary log; check whether the car has a Tiptronic control unit.";
CM_ BO_ 192 "0x0C0. RB Lenkwinkel_1 layout: DLC=2, angle on bits 5..14 (factor 2.5, offset -720) plus sign and status/check bits. Not verified while steering.";
CM_ BO_ 1272 "0x4F8. Sent by the VCU (raw bytes). Signals unknown. OPEN (986 #8): not in the stationary log; check whether it exists on this car.";
CM_ BO_ 1376 "0x560. Signals unknown, raw bytes only. OPEN (986 #8): not in the stationary log; check whether it exists on this car.";
CM_ BO_ 1952 "0x7A0. Sent by the VCU instead of the DME (raw bytes). Signals unknown. Standard payload: 85 0C 00 03 00 00 FF 02 (constant in the log).";
CM_ SG_ 640 RPM "Engine speed shown by the tachometer; the VCU sends the motor power here (VCU-REQ-005).";
